WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.180
I’m just one person out of 10,000 descendants.

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:09.680
I want them just to keep the process of listening to create just that.

3
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:17.280
What I discovered in communicating with the administration at the president’s office, in particular, that there were other descendants that,

4
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.500
of course, I wasn’t privy to knowing that they existed or they were communicating with them.

5
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.600
And I stumbled on that.

6
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:31.240
So we made sure that everybody who was known to be a representative of a group had something so that . . . Hey,

7
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.280
you a part of this and you a valued member.

8
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:38.360
So, the transparency—let us communicate with us about what’s going on.

9
00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.960
In fact, who are the descendants?

10
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.140
So that we can communicate with each other.

11
00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:45.220
Unless somebody says, “Hey, for privacy reasons, they don’t want anybody else to know.”

12
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:53.760
Also, there’s got to be ways that Georgetown and the Jesuits can find ways to almost create opportunities for capacity.

13
00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.720
What I mean by that, say with research and archives, that we’re not coming always to them.

14
00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:03.720
We have people who are PhDs, graduate students, and the like who could really participate in some of the research, too.

15
00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:04.760
In fact, they are.

16
00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:11.080
We are, in terms of . . . Also, a lot of things related to the GU272,

17
00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:20.320
we can be a part of, lecturing and developing other academic and nonacademic programs related to GU272.

18
00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:28.400
In addition to, obviously, that there were other things, in fact, that the descendants spoke about at the gathering on last Tuesday.

19
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.760
That list is kind of extensive.

20
00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:35.140
But I think the openness, the transparency, and they’re willing to say, “Hey.

21
00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:40.620
Receive us as people worthy of being included,” is the beginning.
